================================================================================
CHALLENGE : THE DATA AGGREGATOR (CyclicBarrier)
================================================================================
SCENARIO: You have 3 different services (Auth, Database, Cache) that must
all finish "Loading" before the server can print "SYSTEM READY".
Unlike a Latch, the Barrier is for threads waiting for EACH OTHER.

1. CLASS: 'ServiceModule' (implements Runnable)
   - CONSTRUCTOR: Takes 'String serviceName' and 'CyclicBarrier barrier'.
   - 'run()' LOGIC:
        * Print: serviceName + " is loading resources..."
        * Thread.sleep(random time); // Simulate different loading speeds.
        * ACTION: Call 'barrier.await()'. (Wait for the other 2 services).
        * PRINT: serviceName + " is now LIVE."

2. CLASS: 'SystemLauncher' (Main)
   - TOOL: 'CyclicBarrier barrier = new CyclicBarrier(3, () ->
           System.out.println(">>> ALL SYSTEMS READY: STARTING SERVER <<<"));'
   - EXECUTION:
        * Start 3 'ServiceModule' threads with different names.

EXPECTATION: The "SYSTEM READY" message will ONLY print after the last
thread calls await(). Then all threads proceed to the "LIVE" message.
================================================================================